1.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;This document serves as the Request For Quote (RFQ) for commercial services prepared in accordance with Revolutionary FAR Overhaul (RFO) Federal Acquisition Regulation (FAR) 12.202(b)(1). This is the only solicitation that will be issued; we are requesting quotes, and no written solicitation will follow. Please refer to &quot;W912J327Q1001&rdquo; on all quotes that are submitted to the Government for this combined synopsis/solicitation. This solicitation is issued as a Request for Quotation (RFQ) and incorporates all provisions and clauses in effect through the Federal RFO FAR. All responsible sources are invited to submit a quote. 
&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; 
a.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;IMPORTANT Notices for Quoters 

 i.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;Governing Regulations: This solicitation is governed by the regulations effective July 1, 2026, under Class Deviation 2026-O0028 &ndash; Revolutionary FAR Overhaul (RFO) Part 12, and DFARS 212. 

 ii.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;Business Classification: This acquisition is designated as a total small business set-aside. The North American Industry Classification System (NAICS) code is 722310 &ndash; Food Service Contractors, and the Product Service Code (PSC) is PSC M1FD &ndash; Operation of Dining Facilities. The standard size for this NAICS is $47,000,000. 

 iii.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;System for Award Management (SAM) Registration: To be considered for an award, all quoters must have an active registration in the System for Award Management (SAM) at https://sam.gov/.&nbsp; 

 iv.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;The contracting officer will verify the prospective awardee&#39;s representations and certifications in SAM upon receipt of quote and also prior to issuing an award. Failure to maintain SAM registration shall result in the quoter being deemed ineligible for award. 

 v.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;Payment Instructions: For details regarding payment and acceptance, please refer to DFARS Clause 252.232-7006 WIDE AREA WORKFLOW PAYMENT INSTRUCTIONS (JAN 2023), which is incorporated in full below. Please note that all payments will be 30 days after an invoice is submitted via Wide Area Work Flow (WAWF) and accepted by the Government. Invoices can only be submitted after a completion/acceptance of DFAC Services.&nbsp; 

 vi.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;Applicable Commercial Clauses: The following commercial provisions and clauses are applicable to this acquisition: 
1.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;FAR 52.212-1: Instructions to Offerors &mdash;Commercial Products and Commercial Services (FEB 2026)&nbsp; 
2.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;FAR 52.212-4: Terms and Conditions&mdash;Commercial Products and Commercial Services (FEB 2026)&nbsp; 

 vii.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;Additional Terms: No other terms and conditions have been deemed necessary for this acquisition beyond what is listed in this RFQ.&nbsp; 

 viii.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;52.232-18 Availability of Funds (April 1984)&nbsp; 

 Funds are not presently available for this contract. The Government&rsquo;s obligation under this contract is contingent upon the availability of appropriated funds from which payment for contract purposes can be made. No legal liability on the part of the Government for any payment may arise until funds are made available to the Contracting Officer for this contract and until the Contractor receives notice of such availability, to be confirmed in writing by the Contracting Officer. 

 b.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;SITE VISIT DETAILS: An optional site visit will be held at the Regional Training Institute (RTI). 

 When: December 1, 2026, at 11:00 AM Mountain Standard Time (MST) 
Location: 21A Bataan Blvd, Santa Fe, NM 87508. &nbsp; 

 You must pre-register via email at dangela.l.parsons.civ@army.mil with the following information to attend.&nbsp; 
1.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;Provide full name, date of birth, state that driver&rsquo;s license was issued, country of citizenship (if not US list country of citizenship), phone number and company for each person attending the site visit.&nbsp; 
2.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;Pre-registration must be completed no later than November 24, 2026 at 11:00 AM MST.&nbsp; 

 c.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;QUESTIONS AND INQUIRIES: Please submit all questions and inquiries via email to Dangela Parsons at dangela.l.parsons.civ@army.mil no later than December 3, 2026, at 11:00 AM MST. Questions received after this time may not be acknowledged or answered.&nbsp; 

 d.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;QUOTE SUBMISSION: Please submit your quote via email to the points of contact listed above no later than December 11, 2026, at 11:00 AM MST. It is the quoter&#39;s responsibility to monitor SAM.gov for any questions and answers documents posted as well as amendments posted for this requirement. Submit quotations to Dangela Parsons at dangela.l.parsons.civ@army.mil 

 e.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;LATE QUOTES: Any quote received after the exact date and time specified for receipt shall be treated as non-conforming, shall not be evaluated, and shall be excluded from consideration for award 
f.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; 
g.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;It is the quoter&rsquo;s responsibility to ensure the Government receives their quote before the deadline. 

 h.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;QUOTE CONFORMITY AND COMPLETENESS: Quoters are responsible for submitting a complete and conforming quote that addresses all submission requirements outlined in this solicitation. The Government shall evaluate quotes strictly in accordance with the instructions and criteria specified herein. Quote submissions that fail to provide all required documents, forms, attachments, or technical information shall be deemed non-conforming, will not be evaluated and shall not be considered for award. 
